  "details": "I am not sure if this only relates to the local users framerate, or possibly a framerate mismatch between the local user and whoever is controlling the object, but I've found that when using an \"Uncapped\" framerate, objects will stutter like crazy depending on how far away you are from them. The closer you get, and the higher your framerate(?), the more you will notice the stutter.\n\nIn the clip below you can clearly see the difference between the capped (62 fps) and uncapped (170-210 fps):\n\nhttps://streamable.com/7r254u\n\nAnd here is another (uncapped/unknown fps) set of clips that better show off the difference that distance from the object creates:\n\nhttps://streamable.com/60uhz1\n\nhttps://streamable.com/a07hj7\n\nCapping the framerate is the only thing I've solidly tested, distance stuttering might just be a side effect of how the interpolation of distant objects is handled, and the \"mismatching\" framerate is just a theory that I haven't yet tested. Although, it sounds like it could be true based on other users telling me that they've fixed the stuttering they had while sitting in the seats by the person in the seat locking their framerate to 120 to match the drivers fps.\n\nUpdate: Someone on Twitter also commented that it looks like an issue with Unity's update loops?\n\nThey're saying that a search for 'unity camera jitter' apparently shows a lot of similar cases.",
